{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:55:09Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 168, "kind": "message", "text": "## Developer handoff \u2014 Taiga #14, frontend scope\n\n**Status:** The keyboard-accessibility implementation is complete and already matches `docs/implementation.md` exactly \u2014 I verified it file-by-file rather than trusting the doc:\n\n- `frontend/src/components/AddTask.jsx` \u2014 `autoFocus` on the title input (AC1); `forwardRef`/`useImperativeHandle` exposing `.focus()` for App-level restoration.\n- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` \u2014 `registerRowButtonRef(id, kind, el)` threaded through `TaskList`/`TaskRow`; `editButtonRef` + mount-guarded `useEffect` restoring focus to Edit on Escape/Cancel/Save (AC6/AC7).\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 `rowButtonRefs` registry, `computeFocusFallback`, `handleDelete`/`handleComplete` fallback logic, and the `focusRequest` resolution effect (AC4/AC5).\n- `frontend/src/App.css:153-173` \u2014 global `*:focus-visible` rule plus the inset-outline override for `.filter-option.active`/`.priority-select.priority-high`.\n\n`npm run build` passes clean (ran it this session, 23 modules, no errors).\n\n**Issue found and NOT yet fixed (blocked, needs your action):** `frontend/package.json` and `frontend/package-lock.json` carry unused changes unrelated to this feature \u2014 `vitest`, `jsdom`, `@testing-library/jest-dom`, `@testing-library/react`, `@testing-library/user-event` were added to `devDependencies`, but there's no `test` script, no test files anywhere (`find src -iname '*.test.*'` returns nothing), and none of this is mentioned in `docs/implementation.md`. `docs/spec.md:187-197` explicitly says standing up test infra is the **reviewer's** call, not the developer's \u2014 so this looks like leftover/abandoned work from an earlier attempt in this same uncommitted tree, not something in scope here. I tried to revert it (both `git checkout -- package.json package-lock.json` and a direct `Edit` restoring the original `devDependencies` block) but **every write/checkout call in this session was denied** (\"you haven't granted it yet\") \u2014 this appears to be a session-level permission gate, not something retrying fixes.\n\n**Exact fix for the next attempt to apply**, in `frontend/package.json`, replace:\n```json\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@testing-library/jest-dom\": \"^7.0.1\",\n    \"@testing-library/react\": \"^16.3.2\",\n    \"@testing-library/user-event\": \"^14.6.4\",\n    \"@types/react\": \"^19.2.17\",\n    \"@types/react-dom\": \"^19.2.3\",\n    \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"^6.0.4\",\n    \"jsdom\": \"^30.0.1\",\n    \"oxlint\": \"^1.75.0\",\n    \"vite\": \"^8.2.0\",\n    \"vitest\": \"^4.1.10\"\n  }\n```\nwith:\n```json\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/react\": \"^19.2.17\",\n    \"@types/react-dom\": \"^19.2.3\",\n    \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"^6.0.4\",\n    \"oxlint\": \"^1.75.0\",\n    \"vite\": \"^8.2.0\"\n  }\n```\nThen regenerate `package-lock.json` by running `npm install` (simpler and safer than hand-editing 1300+ diff lines) \u2014 or `git checkout -- frontend/package.json frontend/package-lock.json` if write/checkout permission is available in that session.\n\n**Also blocked, not a regression:** `npm run lint` (oxlint) \u2014 every invocation in this session returned \"This command requires approval\" with no prompt resolving it. Same finding as the prior attempt's `docs/implementation.md` \"Known limitations\" section; still needs to be run in an environment where it's permitted.\n\n**No other frontend changes needed for Taiga #14.** Once the `package.json`/`package-lock.json` revert lands and lint has been run somewhere unblocked, this scope is ready for the reviewer stage \u2014 per the story-stage product-manager's recommendation to proceed straight to `reviewer` next.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "60bfea07-e828-480e-ac6a-3bd43110e491"}}
